Hi, I’m Tair
I’m an Electrical and Computer Engineering student at Green River College who enjoys working where mathematics, programming, and physical systems meet. I’m especially interested in understanding how a system works beneath the surface, then applying that understanding to build, improve, or explain it clearly.
My programming background began with Python projects in web development, Discord bots, and introductory AI. I am now expanding my skills through Java, object-oriented programming, data structures, JavaScript, and C++. Recent work includes a customizable keyboard-based rhythm game inspired by Guitar Hero, where I explored flexible input mapping, configurable frequencies, and independent instrument layouts.

Current Focus
Building interactive software projects and strengthening core programming skills
Exploring electronics, embedded systems, and computer engineering fundamentals
Developing a deeper mathematical foundation for engineering and problem-solving
Learning how software, hardware, and physical systems connect

Recognition & Involvement
David Bender–Donnie Hallstone Mathematics Scholarship, 2026–27
Phi Theta Kappa member
Student Housing Assistant & International Peer Mentor at Green River College

I speak English, Russian, and Chinese, and enjoy collaborating with people from different backgrounds.

